From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:16:03 +0900
Subject: Android host: only the device panel turns the phone

The phone turned whenever a configuration carried a quarter turn or a mode across its orientation,
and the turn was relative (upright to landscape and back). Clients resend the whole output state,
and a rotation saved in kwinoutputconfig.json (Rotated270 on the G100 S) came back with it, so the
phone turned over and over without anyone touching it. Now the phone's orientation is the user's
setting in the device panel only: Android turns its window, the host offers the turned size, and
the output takes it as any host resize. A configuration that would turn the phone is ignored (with
any Android size or refresh change carried with it), and the phone output never takes a transform,
whatever a configuration carries.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-05
X-Rungic-Status: Pending
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:display.geometry
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/50
Origin: vendor
